# Dramatic Accusation on a creature whose owner is not its controller: Bot1's Control Magic takes Bot2's Ornithopter, then Bot1 enchants it with
# Dramatic Accusation (tapped as the Aura enters). "{U}{U}: Shuffle enchanted creature into its owner's library" puts it into Bot2's library, its
# owner's (CR 108.3, 400.3), not Bot1's: Bot2's library is shuffled and Bot1's is not, and both Auras, their creature gone, go to Bot1's graveyard (CR 704.5m).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Control Magic
Dramatic Accusation
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Control Magic.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dramatic Accusation.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Library.Count = 12
? Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Dramatic Accusation.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Library.Count = 13
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot2.Shuffles = 1
Bot1.Shuffles = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Dramatic Accusation; Control Magic
